        <groundspeak:log id="684649503">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP215 Edmonton&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We found nearby parking and walked over.  Memories of context photos made this a speedy find.  Mrs Shark then headed over to the cap in Borden Park while Mr Shark brought the vehicle to a closer parking spot.  Now I see there was better parking than either of the places we parked that would have served better for both caps.  The joys of exploring unfamiliar places but we got the job done.  Thanks, ofth.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683366584">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP215 Edmonton&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We enjoyed a really nice walk in Borden Park tonight with the geodawg.  :)  My goal was the 2 brass caps, GJ's was to tag along for the caps and do some Pokémon-ing and the geodawg was just happy to be in a park and walking.  With many Poke-stops and starts along the way this was our first cap target.  The only one tonight that I didn't have to consult the context pics.  :p  Found easily, pics taken and we turned around to head back to the parking lot and the other park cap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TFTBC OFTH!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681367073">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-26T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP215 Edmonton

Grabbed a few more BCPs today on the way to work. Walked from the cap in Borden Park. Nobody at the adjacent bus stop and the drivers in the road didn't seem to pay any attention to me. 

Thanks outforthehunt for another BCP. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680217723">
